{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01HuW3GdVLPCLVgdXcepyBsv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI (mage-claude-orchestrator), and verifies parity through differential testing against Homebrew GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (per-utility packages), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `pkg/sys/` (syscall abstractions), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `magefiles/` (build targets, excluded from generation).\n\n**Current state**: `pkg/testutils/` has source code on the working branch (difftest.go, runner.go). Code for pkg/sys, pkg/format, cmd/ts, cmd/wc, cmd/cat, cmd/sponge exists at generation-merged tags but not on the working branch. No source code exists for pkg/format/ or pkg/sys/ on the current branch.\n\n**Current release (00.0)**: Foundational infrastructure. Four use cases:\n- uc001-magefiles — excluded from generation (DD7)\n- uc002-format — spec complete, code not started\n- uc003-sys — spec complete, code not started\n- uc004-testutils — **already has source code** (difftest.go, runner.go)\n\n## Priority Analysis\n\nOf the remaining release 00.0 use cases, uc002-format (pkg/format) and uc003-sys (pkg/sys) need code. pkg/format comes first alphabetically (P8 tie-breaker). Its size formatting and color output capabilities are independent of pkg/sys, so no blocking dependency. Column alignment (which may depend on terminal width from pkg/sys) is deferred to a follow-up task.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"pkg/format: size formatting and ANSI color output (rel00.0-uc002-format)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - docs/ARCHITECTURE.yaml (pkg/format/ component -- capabilities, design decisions, technology choices)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/ (locate and read the PRD for pkg/format; filename follows pattern prd[NNN]-format.yaml)\n      - docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc002-format.yaml (use case for the format package)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/format/size.go\n        action: create\n        note: Human-readable byte size formatting for binary and SI units\n      - path: pkg/format/color.go\n        action: create\n        note: ANSI color code definitions and file-type colorization\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Implement human-readable byte size formatting with binary (1024-based) units matching GNU coreutils --human-readable output, per the pkg/format PRD size-formatting requirements\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Implement human-readable byte size formatting with SI (1000-based) units matching GNU coreutils --si output, per the pkg/format PRD size-formatting requirements\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Implement ANSI color code definitions and a colorization function for standard file types (directory, symlink, executable, pipe, socket, block device, char device, setuid, setgid, sticky, other-writable), per the pkg/format PRD color requirements\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Implement ANSI SGR reset and color disable toggle so callers can enable or disable color output, per the pkg/format PRD color requirements\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use only Go standard library for pkg/format -- no external dependencies. golang.org/x/sys is reserved for pkg/sys per ARCHITECTURE.yaml.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Follow all design decisions in the pkg/format PRD verbatim. Copy struct definitions, function signatures, and naming conventions from the PRD.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Copyright header on every .go file: Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved. SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\"\n      - id: D4\n        text: \"Package name is format, matching the ARCHITECTURE.yaml component name pkg/format/.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"go build ./pkg/format/... compiles with no errors\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go vet ./pkg/format/... reports no issues\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Binary (1024-based) size formatting handles: 0 bytes, values at exact unit boundaries (1024, 1048576), and values up to the exabyte range\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"SI (1000-based) size formatting handles: 0 bytes, values at exact unit boundaries (1000, 1000000), and values up to the exabyte range\"\n      - id: AC5\n        text: \"Color output produces valid ANSI SGR escape sequences for all standard file types listed in R3\"\n      - id: AC6\n        text: \"When color is disabled, colorization functions return the input string without any ANSI escape sequences\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":19716,"cache_read_input_tokens":19292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":19716},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a28f80a9-4296-4d31-a482-e0a926774f3c","uuid":"665a88a6-dee0-4e0f-b646-0891eb49df9a"}
